{"version":"2.1.0","runs":[{"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true,"toolExecutionNotifications":[{"descriptor":{"id":"Syntax error"},"level":"warning","message":{"text":"Syntax error at line /Users/scep/greg-wt/odos-cleanup/infra/optimism-mainnet/compose-up.sh:91:\n `<` was unexpected"}},{"descriptor":{"id":"Syntax error"},"level":"warning","message":{"text":"Syntax error at line /Users/scep/greg-wt/odos-cleanup/infra/optimism-mainnet/configs/driver.toml.tmpl:7:\n `app-data-fetching-enabled = true\norderbook-url = \"http://orderbook\"\ntx-gas-limit = \"30000000\"\n\n# Skip eth_createAccessList preflight before settlement simulation.\n#\n# Original (pre-eRPC) rationale: public OP RPCs (publicnode, ankr) return\n# `\"storageKeys\": null` for empty entries on complex traces, which trips\n# alloy's strict deserializer in the driver and surfaces as a confusing\n# Simulation Revert error.\n#\n# Phase 4 audit M-4 (2026-05-19) — partial fix landed, full re-enable\n# deferred:\n#\n# AL simulation is a defense-in-depth check (predicts on-chain settle()\n# success more accurately than bare eth_call). Disabling it means we\n# trust the bare-call simulation alone. Pre-eRPC this was a real risk:\n# any single hostile upstream answering eth_call with a fake success\n# could trick the driver into broadcasting a tx that reverts on real\n# chain (cost: gas only, but a sustained attack costs the 0.02 ETH\n# driver budget).\n#\n# Post-#130 (eRPC + 2-of-3 consensus on eth_call): the bare-call path\n# IS now consensus-protected. The marginal value of AL preflight on top\n# of consensus is much smaller — AL catches a narrow case where\n# simulation passes but settle() fails due to mid-tx storage changes\n# (rare on OP given 2s block times + our access-pattern).\n#\n# Net: keeping disable=true here is now LOW residual risk. Flipping to\n# false requires either (a) an alloy version that tolerates null\n# storageKeys, OR (b) eRPC response normalization mapping null → [].\n# Tracked as a 